<title>USA: Tribune closes Renaissance purchase.</title>
<headline>Tribune closes Renaissance purchase.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tribune Co Tuesday completed its $1.13-billion acquisition of Renaissance Communications Corp, making the media conglomerate the nation's second-largest television station operator.</p>
<p>Tribune picked up six stations that make up Renaissance's broadcast holdings, including television stations in Dallas, Indianapolis and Miami. It now has 16 network-affiliated television stations along with superstation WGN-TV.</p>
<p>Tribune is expected to sell either the Miami station or its newspaper in Ft. Lauderdale within 12 months to comply with Federal Communications Commission regulations.</p>
<p>The company's shares closed up 1-1/4 Tuesday at 42-1/8.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
